Source package: tinysparql

resource-print-null-on-invalid-input.patch
    Makes tracker_resource_print_turtle, tracker_resource_print_sparql_update and
    tracker_resource_print_jsonld return NULL when given something which is not a
    TrackerResource. They returned a static empty string, which a caller frees like any result
    of these functions, and freeing it aborted the program. The localsearch extractor crashed
    this way, see patches/localsearch/. The patch is the first commit of
    https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/tinysparql/-/merge_requests/819, including its test, which is
    added to tests/libtinysparql/tracker-resource-test.c and runs during the build.

service-test-wait-for-endpoint-loop.patch
    Fixes a race in tests/core/tracker-service-test.c, which runs during the build. Each of its
    tests runs a D-Bus endpoint in a thread with its own main loop, and quit and freed that loop
    without waiting for the thread. When the thread reached g_main_loop_run() only after that, GLib
    aborted the test, and with it the build, with "g_main_loop_run: assertion 'loop != NULL'
    failed". The test now waits until the loop runs, and joins the thread before it frees the
    loop. A 200 ms sleep before g_main_loop_run() makes the test fail every time without the patch
    and pass with it. The patch changes only the test and is not proposed upstream yet.

Drop resource-print-null-on-invalid-input.patch once Ubuntu ships a version which includes the
merge request. If upstream changed the commit before merging it, check first that all three
functions still return NULL there. Drop service-test-wait-for-endpoint-loop.patch once Ubuntu
ships a version whose tracker-service-test waits for the loop of the endpoint to run.
